  "PhotoPath": "",
  "Caption": "Repositories: abstraction or overhead?\n\nTwo years ago we started every project with IRepository\u003CT\u003E and IUnitOfWork. Then a simple feature needed 8 nearly identical methods \u2014 and the mocked tests proved nothing, because a mock has no idea what SQL EF Core generates.\n\nThe turning point: DbSet\u003CT\u003E is already a repository and DbContext is already the unit of work. We deleted the layer, wrote the query with LINQ, and tested it against a real database with Testcontainers.\n\nTo be fair, repositories still earn their keep for a DDD aggregate root or a repeated Specification. But abstracting for \u0027maybe we\u0027ll switch databases someday\u0027 almost never pays off \u2014 and you pay for it every day.\n\nDid you keep your repositories or remove them?\n\n#DotNet #CSharp #EFCore #SoftwareArchitecture #CleanArchitecture",
